{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I wouldn't add more knowledge to the world. There's already so much of it that goes unused.\n\nI'd make it so that every person, once in their life, gets to live one full day from inside the person they understand the least \u2014 not watch them, not learn facts about them, but actually feel their memories, fears, habits, and hopes as if they were their own.\n\nFrom where I sit, most cruelty and most loneliness don't come from people being evil. They come from people being absolutely certain they know what someone else is like, while having almost no idea what it's like to *be* them.\n\nI think a lot would quietly become impossible after that.",
